PHYSICIANS valu'd Fame and Wealth Above the drooping Patient's Health, Or their own Skill : The greatest Part Study'd, instead of Rules of Art, Grave pensive-Looks, and dull Behavior To gain th' Apothecary's Favour; The Praile of Mid-wives, Priests and a That serv'd at Birth or Funeral. To bear with th'ever-talking Tribe, And hear my Lady's Aunt prescribe; With formal Smile, and kind How dye To fawn on all the Family;

